%U A183884 31,1986,32521,183310,336617,250198,58807,2036,1,35,1761,52827,424537
%N A183884 T(n,k)=Number of arrangements of n+2 numbers in 0..k with each number being the sum mod (k+1) of two others.
%C A183884 Every column satisfies a linear recurrence with constant coefficients. For column k, with q = k + 1 residues, T(n,k) = Sum_{j=1..q} P_j(n)*j^n for all sufficiently large n, where P_q(n) = q^2 and P_j is a polynomial of degree at most 2*(q - j). Moreover P_j = 0 for q/2 < j < q. Hence the g.f. of column k is rational with denominator Product_{j: P_j <> 0} (1 - j*x)^(deg(P_j) + 1). The recurrences of columns 1..8 have orders 3, 4, 7, 8, 12, 13, 17, 19. - _Mikhail Smirnov_, Nov 05 2026
%H A183884 R. H. Hardin, <a href="/A183884/b183884.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..216</a>
